      "message": "Hi, here is the response I was asked to provide. This comes from the Android security council:\n\n\u003e This falls in the broad category of URL/URI (in practice used interchangeably) parsing disparities, which has been extensively discussed in the security community. This is an internet-wide problem and is not specific to Android.\n\u003e\n\u003e Every library that handles URLs has its own philosophy about permissiveness, compatibility, error handling, and intended use-cases. Changing the behavior of core/java/android/webkit/URLUtil.java will break compatibility with its current users, while also not improve security for any future users due to parsing disparities with their ultimate use-cases.\n\nSorry if this is not the response you wanted. Unfortunately, we cannot accept this patch.",
